  First of all, I agree with those who says the version number should
be 4.0 instead of 3.1 - it seems a *very* different game; but *great*,
from what I've tried so far.  Having monsters behave more offensive
and intelligent really adds a whole new aspect to the game ...

  However, I have a small bug report and some questions.  The version
I've been playing was the executable MS-DOS uploaded to wuarchive.

bug	-  rock moles (perhaps other rock eaters too?) are not
	displayed when they enter the scenario: it just says "The rock
	mole bites", and you'll have to ^R redraw to see the little
	bugger.

bug?	- I quaffed from a fountain and briefly saw all objects on the
	level, like in 3.0j.  However, they didn't disappear but stayed
	on the screen.  When I got to some of them they disappeared as
	I moved onto that coordinate, because some monster had removed
	them since they were drawn.  BTW, even ^R insists on redrawing
	those objects (hence the questionmark; is this a *feature*?)

bug	- Paid in a shop a got a "error in shopkeeper <bill?>" or
	something and shortly after the game froze.

Q	- Do you really have to walk directly into walls (not just pass
	them) in dark rooms to map them?

Q	- Does spellbooks really last forever (or at least more than
	once) ?

Q	- On the technical side: how much environment space do you
	need?  I had to enlarge it quite much to avoid a runtime error
	(runtime error?  That could be done prettier).

  I've been reading almost all postings here in r.g.h since 3.1
emerged and don't remember any of these issues coming up (except the
spellbook and dark room part, but that wasn't any authorative answers)

